2,1,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
3,1,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
4,1,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
5,1,1,talk,Asuka,,"We need a fair system that doesn't create unnecessary friction among neighbors. To understand the history and current usage, I'll look into the five years of association minutes and last year's complaint log entries.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Yumi,,"I want to make sure everyone is happy! To see if the current spots are actually being used and if people are feeling unfair, I'll check the sticker register and the daily riders, plus the complaint log.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Ryuji,,I want to understand the physical reality of the parking area and how people actually behave. I'll look into the morning departures watched from the entrance and the rain exposure along the parking rows.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Since we always end up arguing about money without any actual data, I'll be the rational one. I'll check the building account's two-year ledger and the treasurer's handover file on cash collections.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Toshio,,"I agree that we need a sustainable approach. To understand the administrative burden and how other areas handle this, I will look into the account from the neighbouring block's secretary and the treasurer's handover file.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Asuka,,"It seems we have a good spread of data. @Shunichi and @Toshio are focusing on the finances, while @Ryuji is looking at the physical layout. I believe the historical context I'm seeking will complement these findings.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shunichi"",""Toshio"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Yumi,,I agree! It's great that we're all looking at different things. I'm really hoping we can find a way to make everyone smile and feel that the system is fair for everyone!,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Ryuji,,"It is important that we don't rely on assumptions. By observing the actual flow of movement and the condition of the spaces, we can identify the root causes of any friction before proposing a solution.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Shunichi,,"Exactly. While optimism and ""feelings"" are all well and good, they don't pay the bills or solve deficits. I'll provide the hard numbers so we can stop guessing and start deciding.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Toshio,,"Numbers are useful, but the process of maintaining them is where most systems fail. I am interested in the actual labor involved in the management, not just the final balance.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Asuka,,I agree with @Toshio. A system that is too complex to manage will only lead to resentment. We must ensure the final rule is simple enough to maintain without causing stress to the association.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Yumi,,"That's a great point, @Asuka! If it's too complicated, people might get confused and upset. Let's keep it simple and friendly so everyone can get along!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Ryuji,,"Simplicity is a virtue, but it shouldn't come at the cost of accuracy. If we ignore the physical constraints of the space, even a simple rule will fail when people actually try to park.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Shunichi,,"Accuracy is a fine goal, @Ryuji, but let's not over-engineer this. A perfect map is useless if the building is broke. I'll let you know if our budget can even support your ""physical constraints.""","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Toshio,,"Budget is one thing, but the time spent on administration is another cost entirely. I want to ensure we don't create a role that becomes a burden for a single person.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Asuka,,I believe we have covered all the necessary angles. Let's proceed to review our findings. I hope the data reveals a path that preserves the harmony of our community while solving the shortage.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Yumi,,I'm so excited to see what we find! I really hope we can find a solution that makes everyone feel included and happy. Let's do our best for the neighborhood!,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Ryuji,,I agree. Let us move forward. I will analyze the observations of the morning rush and the layout to see if the physical arrangement itself is the source of the problem.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Let's get on with it then. I'll be waiting to see if the numbers actually support the idealistic visions you all have. Try not to get too lost in the ""harmony"" of it all.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Toshio,,"I will focus on the practicalities of the workload. Once we have the data, we can determine a system that is not only fair but actually sustainable for whoever has to manage it.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
